1
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:08,940
Futaba-chan!

2
00:00:10,790 --> 00:00:15,010
The donut shop in front of the station is having a 100-yen sale.

3
00:00:15,930 --> 00:00:17,990
Wanna stop by with me?

4
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:20,040
Yuuri...

5
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:25,360
Sure.

6
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:30,260
Today, I might lose...

7
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:33,400
...a very dear friend.

8
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:38,180
The world has fallen in love

9
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:41,850
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

10
00:00:41,850 --> 00:00:45,140
I just want to understand you

11
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:49,520
Won't you open up to me?

12
00:00:56,450 --> 00:01:00,660
A fumbled exchange of words leaves a little taste of regret

13
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:04,000
Enough to make me cry

14
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,340
I want to link my racing emotions to the beat of my heart

15
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:16,470
and put it all in tune

16
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:22,310
I lost sight of everything but my goal

17
00:01:22,310 --> 00:01:25,980
and had something important fade away

18
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:32,230
Let's start all over

19
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:37,360
The world has fallen in love

20
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:40,620
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

21
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:44,200
I want to know everything about you

22
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:48,370
Won't you tell me more?

23
00:01:48,370 --> 00:01:52,000
One inch feels like a million miles

24
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,920
as the days just seem to race by

25
00:01:55,590 --> 00:01:59,340
I won't and can't ever forget

26
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:02,600
this brightest page of my life.

27
00:02:11,940 --> 00:02:16,360
Today is the day I will definitely, absolutely tell Yuuri.

28
00:02:18,530 --> 00:02:19,860
I can say what I want...

29
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:24,830
...but it feels like I'm just going to end up chickening out again.

30
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:30,290
That's it. If I don't tell her today,
I am going to shave my head.

31
00:02:30,290 --> 00:02:31,540
No going back.

32
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:34,710
It's Murao-san!

33
00:02:34,710 --> 00:02:37,090
Let's invite Murao-san, too.

34
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:39,470
Murao-san!

35
00:02:39,470 --> 00:02:40,680
Wait!

36
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:44,140
Are you telling me I have to say it in front of her too?

37
00:02:47,270 --> 00:02:50,560
I already decided to shave my head if I didn't tell her today...

38
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:54,570
If I can't today, I don't think I ever will.

39
00:02:56,940 --> 00:02:59,950
So you're seriously hanging out with Makita Yuuri now.

40
00:03:00,450 --> 00:03:01,700
Asumi.

41
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:05,120
What?

42
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:09,660
L-Listen to this! The donut shop by the station is having a 100-yen sale!

43
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:11,210
Wanna check it out?

44
00:03:11,210 --> 00:03:11,960
Huh?

45
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:14,670
You, me, and Futaba-chan. The three of us.

46
00:03:15,630 --> 00:03:16,750
Why?

47
00:03:18,090 --> 00:03:22,220
Sorry I asked out of nowhere.
I'm sure you're busy.

48
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:23,640
I should've figured.

49
00:03:25,970 --> 00:03:28,100
I suppose I'm free.

50
00:03:30,850 --> 00:03:33,440
You really have changed.

51
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:36,570
Thank you.

52
00:03:37,940 --> 00:03:40,570
That's what I've been trying to do.

53
00:03:41,070 --> 00:03:44,240
I'll take those words as a compliment.

54
00:03:45,990 --> 00:03:47,450
Sure.

55
00:03:49,250 --> 00:03:51,210
I focused on trying not to be hated

56
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:54,290
and couldn't express my true feelings.

57
00:03:55,750 --> 00:03:57,590
We were just pretending to be friends

58
00:03:58,090 --> 00:03:59,880
and Kou called me out on it.

59
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:07,010
I'm different now.

60
00:04:08,510 --> 00:04:10,180
I managed to change.

61
00:04:10,810 --> 00:04:12,270
Futaba-chan!

62
00:04:14,150 --> 00:04:17,110
With Yuuri, I'm not pretending.

63
00:04:16,110 --> 00:04:19,940
Murao-san agreed to come! Let's go!

64
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:19,940
She's a truly precious friend.

65
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:25,910
And it's because she's so precious to me that I want to be honest with her.

66
00:04:31,450 --> 00:04:32,790
But still...

67
00:04:32,790 --> 00:04:36,540
Look! Mabuchi-kun lent it to me today!

68
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:37,750
I'm so lucky!

69
00:04:37,750 --> 00:04:41,670
I can't find the right timing to tell her!

70
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:45,800
Say it or shave my head.

71
00:04:47,010 --> 00:04:50,310
But I'm scared! I'm so scared to speak up!

72
00:04:52,770 --> 00:04:53,270
Yuu—

73
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:56,230
Are you okay?

74
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:03,320
My heart feels like it's going to shatter.

75
00:05:06,030 --> 00:05:07,200
But...

76
00:05:08,910 --> 00:05:09,830
Yuuri.

77
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:16,620
There's... something I need to tell you.

78
00:05:18,750 --> 00:05:19,840
Um...

79
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:27,090
The truth is, I...

80
00:05:30,010 --> 00:05:32,560
...I also like him.

81
00:05:33,470 --> 00:05:35,690
I like Kou.

82
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:42,730
I fell in love with the boy you liked.

83
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:44,110
Sorry.

84
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:51,410
You too, Futaba-chan?

85
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:57,210
He's so cool and handsome, isn't he?

86
00:05:57,210 --> 00:05:59,920
I think you two need glasses.

87
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:02,920
What? He totally is!

88
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:02,920
Huh?

89
00:06:03,420 --> 00:06:05,800
What don't you like about Mabuchi-kun?

90
00:06:04,210 --> 00:06:07,010
Was this even a possibility?

91
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:07,880
He acts like a spoiled brat.

92
00:06:08,340 --> 00:06:11,350
I wish I'd just said it sooner.

93
00:06:11,890 --> 00:06:13,890
Oh, but now...

94
00:06:13,890 --> 00:06:19,060
Futaba-chan, you and Mabuchi-kun are already really close, so I've got no chance.

95
00:06:19,060 --> 00:06:21,650
You're wrong! We're not!

96
00:06:21,650 --> 00:06:26,030
Kou already told me he doesn't like me that way.

97
00:06:26,030 --> 00:06:29,280
Huh? Futaba-chan, you've already confessed to him?

98
00:06:29,610 --> 00:06:32,070
N-No, it's not like that.

99
00:06:32,070 --> 00:06:37,790
Just, I recently found out that we actually both liked each other back in middle school.

100
00:06:40,330 --> 00:06:46,340
But when we met again, he straight up
told me that it was all in the past.

101
00:06:46,710 --> 00:06:48,300
I see.

102
00:06:50,430 --> 00:06:56,560
At first, I felt the same way.
That I didn't like who he'd become.

103
00:07:00,690 --> 00:07:02,100
Alright then.

104
00:07:02,610 --> 00:07:07,070
From here on out, no getting angry no matter who wins.

105
00:07:14,950 --> 00:07:17,750
Oh, I'm going to the bathroom for a bit.

106
00:07:29,010 --> 00:07:31,010
I was so scared.

107
00:07:35,810 --> 00:07:37,430
Yoshioka-san?

108
00:07:38,350 --> 00:07:40,310
I knew I had to tell her,

109
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:44,810
but I couldn't get the words out.

110
00:07:47,070 --> 00:07:48,730
It's finally over.

111
00:07:56,870 --> 00:07:59,620
Futaba-chan likes Mabuchi-kun too.

112
00:08:03,750 --> 00:08:08,550
We both love the same person.

113
00:08:10,550 --> 00:08:15,010
It must've been so hard for her to tell me.

114
00:08:25,150 --> 00:08:29,400
We can both love him, and whoever wins, wins.

115
00:08:41,540 --> 00:08:43,290
I'm back!

116
00:08:43,910 --> 00:08:45,080
Hey.

117
00:08:48,790 --> 00:08:52,260
Yuuri... her eyes are red.

118
00:08:49,590 --> 00:08:52,260
My juice is all gone.

119
00:08:53,130 --> 00:08:54,880
She must have gone to the bathroom...

120
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,180
...to cry.

121
00:09:01,430 --> 00:09:02,350
I...

122
00:09:02,680 --> 00:09:04,190
...am also in love.

123
00:09:05,310 --> 00:09:06,480
With Tanaka-sensei.

124
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:09,480
What?! Where did that even come from?!

125
00:09:10,570 --> 00:09:13,610
Huh? You don't seem all that surprised.

126
00:09:13,610 --> 00:09:16,070
Did you already know?

127
00:09:17,950 --> 00:09:19,120
Um...

128
00:09:19,990 --> 00:09:22,040
I didn't want anyone to know,

129
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:25,040
but she happened to find out.

130
00:09:25,660 --> 00:09:30,500
I was wondering if she had told you already,

131
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:39,220
but it looks like she kept her word and stayed silent.

132
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:45,390
Makita-san's a good girl.

133
00:09:46,690 --> 00:09:53,320
You knew that too. That's why you strained yourself to come clean.

134
00:09:58,950 --> 00:10:06,790
After looking at you two, I thought it might be okay to tell you about my feelings.

135
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:08,750
That's where it came from.

136
00:10:11,290 --> 00:10:12,710
To tell you the truth,

137
00:10:12,710 --> 00:10:18,970
this is the first time I've gone somewhere after school with friends since I entered high school.

138
00:10:20,260 --> 00:10:21,760
Murao-san...

139
00:10:24,310 --> 00:10:27,850
It'll all come down to Mabuchi's decision, anyway.

140
00:10:28,850 --> 00:10:32,730
There's no point in fighting each other over him.

141
00:10:32,730 --> 00:10:36,690
You could both lose, for all we know.

142
00:10:38,110 --> 00:10:40,160
Very true.

143
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:44,030
But even if one of you succeeds,

144
00:10:44,740 --> 00:10:48,830
I'll still be on both of your sides.

145
00:10:48,830 --> 00:10:51,080
Good luck, you two.

146
00:10:52,790 --> 00:10:54,380
Yeah, thanks!

147
00:10:54,380 --> 00:10:55,840
You're the best!

148
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:59,470
That said, you two have some terrible taste.

149
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:17,860
Murao...

150
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:24,030
I heard you weren't coming to our after-finals karaoke party.

151
00:11:24,030 --> 00:11:25,280
Yeah.

152
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:28,200
You haven't gone to a single class gathering.

153
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:29,660
Can't you show your face for once?

154
00:11:31,290 --> 00:11:33,000
I don't feel like going.

155
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,960
It's not like I have any attachment to the class anyway.

156
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:37,960
But...

157
00:11:40,090 --> 00:11:42,470
It's none of your business, Kominato-kun.

158
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:07,870
The sky's already pitch-black.

159
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,830
Girls talk is serious stuff.

160
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:13,290
I'm so glad I told her everything.

161
00:12:14,250 --> 00:12:16,960
Now I can get close to Kou.

162
00:12:22,130 --> 00:12:23,220
Kou?

163
00:12:24,930 --> 00:12:27,430
Why are you here now, of all times?

164
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:30,680
I'm not ready yet...

165
00:12:31,850 --> 00:12:32,730
Okay!

166
00:12:37,110 --> 00:12:38,400
Kou?

167
00:12:39,650 --> 00:12:42,110
Oh, it's the same cat we saw before.

168
00:12:42,110 --> 00:12:45,240
I think he's gotten used to this place.

169
00:12:46,950 --> 00:12:49,490
But doesn't he seem thinner?

170
00:12:49,490 --> 00:12:52,540
Hope he's getting enough to eat.

171
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:55,500
Why not adopt him if you're so worried?

172
00:12:55,500 --> 00:12:59,630
I can't. I'll start to get attached if I take him home.

173
00:13:00,670 --> 00:13:03,220
What's so wrong with that?

174
00:13:04,630 --> 00:13:08,220
The more things you view as precious,

175
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:10,310
the more they weigh you down.

176
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:16,440
See you.

177
00:13:17,350 --> 00:13:18,610
You're getting on a train?

178
00:13:18,610 --> 00:13:21,280
Where are you going this late at night?

179
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:22,820
That's my secret.

180
00:13:27,570 --> 00:13:33,450
The more things you view as precious, the more they weigh you down.

181
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:38,420
What about school and friends?

182
00:13:38,420 --> 00:13:41,050
Does Kou not hold them precious?

183
00:13:44,260 --> 00:13:46,430
Hearing him say something like that,

184
00:13:49,180 --> 00:13:50,300
I can't help but worry.

185
00:14:04,230 --> 00:14:09,370
So here I am following him, but where's he going?

186
00:14:17,790 --> 00:14:19,210
He got off!

187
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:51,700
Hey, a high school girl.

188
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:53,450
She's pretty cute.

189
00:14:56,910 --> 00:15:00,120
Huh? What's up with this place?

190
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:02,290
It's full of young people.

191
00:15:03,590 --> 00:15:04,960
Oh, hey Kou.

192
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:05,840
Sup.

193
00:15:07,510 --> 00:15:12,220
It's Kou... is he friends with those guys?

194
00:15:12,760 --> 00:15:15,470
I wonder why... it's like...

195
00:15:16,010 --> 00:15:18,850
Kou is in a completely different world.

196
00:15:19,390 --> 00:15:20,560
I don't like it.

197
00:15:25,860 --> 00:15:27,530
What are you doing here?

198
00:15:27,530 --> 00:15:30,110
That's what I want to ask you!

199
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:34,450
Where'd you come from, and why are you angry?

200
00:15:34,740 --> 00:15:37,950
Because, uh...

201
00:15:41,170 --> 00:15:44,630
It's almost time for midterms!
Shouldn't you be studying?

202
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:50,670
Kou-kun, you can't let your brain go to waste like that.

203
00:15:51,630 --> 00:15:52,720
Your girl?

204
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:53,800
Hell no.

205
00:15:54,890 --> 00:15:56,890
Mind if I hit on her then?

206
00:15:56,890 --> 00:15:58,770
She's spot-on my type.

207
00:16:00,230 --> 00:16:04,310
She's crude and ill-mannered, eats more
than I do, and has huge feet to boot.

208
00:16:04,310 --> 00:16:06,940
I'm not sure if you can even call her a girl.

209
00:16:06,940 --> 00:16:08,730
Excuse me, what are you talking about?

210
00:16:09,150 --> 00:16:11,860
Nah, I'd say she's quite the girl.

211
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:13,860
Hey there, baby.

212
00:16:13,860 --> 00:16:15,740
Huh? Who are you?

213
00:16:16,030 --> 00:16:18,790
I bet she's really packing.

214
00:16:18,790 --> 00:16:20,290
You with anyone?

215
00:16:20,290 --> 00:16:21,790
Um, well...

216
00:16:22,660 --> 00:16:23,790
Her tits.

217
00:16:29,210 --> 00:16:32,670
Hearing someone say that about my friend

218
00:16:32,670 --> 00:16:34,180
really pisses me off.

219
00:16:35,050 --> 00:16:38,060
Sorry, I'm out for tonight.

220
00:16:55,780 --> 00:17:01,620
Before I knew it, I had run

221
00:16:55,780 --> 00:17:01,620
kudarizaka fumikiri made

222
00:17:01,620 --> 00:17:06,630
all the way down to the train tracks.

223
00:17:01,620 --> 00:17:06,630
atashi wa muchuu de hashitta

224
00:17:02,290 --> 00:17:06,380
Go right here and you'll eventually
reach the train station.

225
00:17:06,630 --> 00:17:12,300
What I found was a train departing,

226
00:17:06,630 --> 00:17:12,300
kono koi wo saegiru you ni

227
00:17:07,290 --> 00:17:09,840
What about you? Aren't you going home?

228
00:17:12,300 --> 00:17:17,180
densha wa sugisatta

229
00:17:12,300 --> 00:17:17,180
taking my love with it.

230
00:17:17,180 --> 00:17:22,850
Distant memories, shining seas.

231
00:17:17,180 --> 00:17:22,850
tooi hi no kioku umi no kagayaki

232
00:17:22,850 --> 00:17:25,730
Seasons pass.

233
00:17:22,850 --> 00:17:25,730
kisetsu wa meguru

234
00:17:25,730 --> 00:17:30,110
Now, I squint up at the clouds.

235
00:17:25,730 --> 00:17:30,110
hikoukigumo ni me wo hosomete

236
00:17:30,110 --> 00:17:35,490
A sunflower swayed in the breeze,

237
00:17:30,110 --> 00:17:35,490
chiisaku yureta himawari

238
00:17:35,490 --> 00:17:41,870
sayonara mo ienai mata

239
00:17:35,490 --> 00:17:41,870
seeing how I couldn't even say goodbye.

240
00:17:41,870 --> 00:17:51,710
We were so tantalizingly close, yet so far apart.

241
00:17:41,870 --> 00:17:51,710
hon no suumiri no sukima de sotto kusuguru itami

242
00:17:45,830 --> 00:17:48,040
Stop following me already!

243
00:17:51,710 --> 00:17:57,260
If only the summer fireworks

244
00:17:51,710 --> 00:17:57,260
manatsu ni kieta hanabi ga

245
00:17:57,260 --> 00:18:03,180
had appeared before my tears...

246
00:17:57,260 --> 00:18:03,180
namida no saki ni utsureba

247
00:17:59,340 --> 00:18:02,180
I'm too frustrated to stop.

248
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:08,600
I will definitely remember.

249
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:08,600
I will kitto omoidasu wa

250
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:11,270
I'm frustrated that it feels like I haven't gotten closer to you at all.

251
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:20,370
Please know that I'll be here, waiting for you.

252
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:20,370
anata ni todoke kono basho de atashi wa matteiru

253
00:18:36,920 --> 00:18:38,130
Thanks.

254
00:18:42,350 --> 00:18:45,770
What are those guys like?

255
00:18:45,770 --> 00:18:48,230
No idea. Don't know them much.

256
00:18:48,230 --> 00:18:51,690
Do you go there often? Why?

257
00:18:51,690 --> 00:18:54,900
It's not a bad place to kill time.

258
00:18:59,490 --> 00:19:02,240
Are you doing something bad?

259
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:06,240
Like drinking or smoking?

260
00:19:10,370 --> 00:19:13,210
I guess some of them do that.

261
00:19:15,960 --> 00:19:18,170
But I don't.

262
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:21,050
I don't really have any desire to.

263
00:19:22,590 --> 00:19:24,430
I just go to talk.

264
00:19:31,770 --> 00:19:34,940
If you want someone to talk with, then I'm right here.

265
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:41,530
A-And Kominato-kun and Yuuri are, too.

266
00:19:41,530 --> 00:19:43,660
You've got plenty of options.

267
00:19:43,660 --> 00:19:48,290
Besides, aren't you just pretending
to be friends with them?

268
00:19:48,290 --> 00:19:49,910
Eat your words!

269
00:19:53,130 --> 00:19:54,790
Hey...

270
00:19:55,420 --> 00:19:58,960
Aren't you a bit too defenseless?
I could just assault you.

271
00:20:00,510 --> 00:20:02,470
What are you saying?

272
00:20:03,590 --> 00:20:07,600
I know you don't see me like that.

273
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:11,480
And I know you'd never do something like that,

274
00:20:11,850 --> 00:20:12,810
so it's fine—

275
00:20:18,150 --> 00:20:20,610
Don't underestimate guys.

276
00:20:20,610 --> 00:20:22,950
You can't even put up a fight.

277
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:26,240
Any guy,

278
00:20:26,830 --> 00:20:29,290
even if he thinks nothing of her,

279
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,160
could assault a girl.

280
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:42,550
Ow!

281
00:20:42,880 --> 00:20:45,010
See? Scary, wasn't it?

282
00:20:45,930 --> 00:20:47,100
A flick?

283
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:50,390
The only reason you didn't just get assaulted

284
00:20:50,390 --> 00:20:53,140
was because it happened to be me.

285
00:20:54,560 --> 00:21:00,320
If you don't want to be scared like that again, don't go to a place like that alone.

286
00:21:03,150 --> 00:21:07,950
Did he do that just to prove a point?

287
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:16,080
Hey, are you crying?

288
00:21:19,460 --> 00:21:22,800
Sorry... I guess I went a bit far.

289
00:21:24,420 --> 00:21:27,680
I really was surprised. Scared, even.

290
00:21:28,890 --> 00:21:32,770
But those aren't the only reasons for my tears.

291
00:21:32,770 --> 00:21:34,480
I'm sorry, okay?

292
00:21:35,940 --> 00:21:40,610
More than that, I'm just ashamed

293
00:21:41,730 --> 00:21:43,190
at how excited it made me.

294
00:21:46,360 --> 00:21:48,030
However...

295
00:21:48,780 --> 00:21:51,160
I'll never tell Kou.

296
00:22:00,790 --> 00:22:05,920
In a town beset by a sudden shower,

297
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:11,300
I say "See you later", and wave goodbye.

298
00:22:11,300 --> 00:22:16,770
As I watch you pass through the ticket gate, I think:

299
00:22:16,770 --> 00:22:22,070
"It never goes according to plan, does it?"

300
00:22:22,070 --> 00:22:31,780
Everything seemed incredibly fragile that day,

301
00:22:31,780 --> 00:22:37,370
but it passed, as days tend to do.

302
00:22:38,540 --> 00:22:47,920
The rails carry you away

303
00:22:47,920 --> 00:22:56,180
leaving me alone on our usual path.

304
00:22:57,310 --> 00:23:06,820
The words I prepared for you are so simple,

305
00:23:06,820 --> 00:23:15,540
so why can't I say them?

306
00:23:17,290 --> 00:23:22,500
Why can't I?

307
00:23:25,050 --> 00:23:40,060
NEXT TIME...

308
00:23:28,420 --> 00:23:31,970
He's got good friends
who'll worry about him now.

309
00:23:33,970 --> 00:23:37,020
I'm sure he'll be able to do his best for you.
